review_comment:
I wavered between this version and the flattened version:
```py
if has_user:
if has_auser:
```

The duplicate imports wouldn't be such a big deal. The duplicate anonymous users wouldn't be such a big deal either, since they are supposed to `__hash__` and `__eq__` to the same thing, but I don't know what people might be stashing on these instances directly, so using the same instance seemed slightly beneficial.

@jacobtylerwalls 
> While I have you @tim-mccurrach, do you agree with my suggestion to move this into docs/internals/contributing so that it nestles itself naturally in the table of contents as mentioned here? 

Yes, I definitely agree. As you say, there's a precedent for content that is how-to-ish in nature within the "contributing to django" section. Likewise, everything within the "how-to" section of the docs is very much about using django. Even without the precedent, I think it's just the more logical place for it too.

