review_comment:
Not against it if you think it helps, I thought third-party apps would define functions based on `django.VERSION` anyway?

e.g.

```python
if django.VERSION >= (6, 1):
   def binary_placeholder_sql(self, value, compiler):
      ...
else:
   def binary_placeholder_sql(self, value)
```

@nessita Turns out this is already possible if you turn on `combine_as_imports`. That is part of the `django` [profile](https://github.com/PyCQA/isort/blob/e6337b2f209a5d468756ebe36247826ba676888b/isort/profiles.py#L14-L19), but you are using the `black` profile (in the `django` project. Oh the irony... :smile:)

Anyway in https://github.com/PyCQA/isort/pull/2470/ I have fixed this issue and also added a test case based on your original report. I hope to release `isort` in the somewhat near future but if you want you can test against our `main` branch already :)

Thanks for the input, always appreciated!

